--- Root-cause check: is griddatan's nearest-neighbor search blind to gamma1? ---
Row 70: nearest-neighbor index for gamma1 in {5e-5, 0.001, 0.01, 0.05}: [976 976 976 976] (all identical: 1)
Squared per-dimension distance contribution for that match: gamma1=3.33e-06, lambda1=5.07e-09, delta=0.333, epsilon=1.49, N1=5.07e-08, N2=1.22e-08
ROOT CAUSE, confirmed: delta and epsilon (raw scale ~10-100) dominate the raw
Euclidean distance by 5-6 orders of magnitude over gamma1 (~1e-5 to 5e-2). Changing
gamma1 across its ENTIRE allowed range barely moves the distance at all, so the
"nearest" training point is selected almost independently of gamma1 -- the fminbnd
search above is optimizing over an essentially flat, noise-dominated loss surface.
This is the mechanism behind both the catastrophic log_error_gamma above AND the
NMSE>1 results already reported in Milestones 6-8: griddatan's raw-feature (not
standardized) distance metric effectively ignores gamma1/lambda1/N1/N2 relative to
delta/epsilon. This is a real, structural limitation of griddatan as actually built
by interpolant.m and carried forward by this project for apples-to-apples parity --
not a bug introduced here.

